name ar-20-bind-blue-high
timeout 600
time 2026-07-27T17:05:00Z
wx wind 9.2 30.9

# THE ARENA, RUNG 20 OF 20. THIS IS NOT A HISTORICAL SCENARIO AND IT DOES NOT DEPICT ONE. It is a
# MEASURING STAND for doc/doctrine-evolution.md - a declared, synthetic cell on which the doctrine
# evolution's gate (S1/S2/S7) can be flown. There is no anchor, no source and no campaign narrative
# behind it, because there is nothing here to be faithful TO: the units, the coordinates and the clock
# are instrument settings. Spec and the whole grid: doc/campaigns/ar-arena.md. Format:
# doc/missions/syntax.md, doc/missions/campaign.md.
#
# WHY THE SECOND TEN EXIST, AND WHAT THEY ADD TO THE FIRST TEN. Rungs 01..10 span doc/doctrine-
# evolution.md 4.2's FIRST axis - initial aspect - across five geometries and ten clocks. 4.2 names
# five axes and each one because the tree MEASURED that it changes the answer; three of them are
# untouched by rungs 01..10 and rungs 11..20 are built to span exactly those three:
#   ENERGY ASYMMETRY   [MESS, 4.2] `split` inverts the entire ranking - f16_base 1085.1 with 7 kills,
#                      every MiG variant negative - where the co-altitude field decides nothing.
#   FORCE RATIO        [MESS, 4.2] the cooperative channel is worth an outcome band on `split`
#                      (940.9 with a kill against 770.0 with none) and NOTHING on `mirror`.
#   WEAPON OBLIGATION  [MESS, 4.2] 0.3 s of binding against 17.3 s, a factor of 58.
# THIS RUNG'S THREE COORDINATES ON THEM:
#   energy  BLUE high and fast - 12 000 m / 500 kt against 6 000 m / 350 kt
#   force   8 blue against 4 red
#   weapon  blue BOUND (AIM-7) / red FREE (R-73 only)
#
# THE FOUR PROPERTIES OF A CELL THAT CAN BE INFORMATIVE (doc/doctrine-evolution.md State E11,
# sections 6, 9, 10 and 2 - each one measured over all 154 committed campaign cells):
#   1 LARGE     - >= 4 aircraft on EVERY graded side. [MESS, E11 6] mean movers by side size:
#                 1 unit 0.44 (41 cells) - 2 units 0.45 (66) - 4 units 1.37 (30) - 8 units 2.00 (6).
#                 THIS RUNG: 8 F-16 in 2 flights of four, 4 MiG-29 in one flight of four.
#   2 OPPOSED   - a hostile FIGHTER in the file. [MESS, E11 9] 8 large cells without one never exceed
#                 2 movers; the means are equal and only the CEILING differs.
#                 THIS RUNG: 4 MiG-29 with 4 x R-73 and NO BVR round and a GCI brief, on the
#                 graded hostile team.
#   3 VISIBLE TO LEVEL M - every graded group declares `objective`s that the run can actually reach.
#                 [MESS, E11 10] 13 cells carry M = 0 on all 24 levers and not one has a single mover.
#                 THIS RUNG: every one of the 12 aircraft carries `survive` plus at least one
#                 contested `kill unit <named>` - never `kill team`, which would need every ground
#                 unit dead as well and could not be met. THE COVERAGE IS COMPLETE AND THAT IS A
#                 CORRECTION TO RUNGS 01..10, not a decoration: doc/missions/verdict.md's
#                 expected-loss rule makes a loss DECISIVE unless another unit named it, and a
#                 decisive loss ENDS the run. [MESS, pass 1 of this ten with rungs 01..10's partial
#                 assignment] ar-16 exited 1 truncated at t = 149.2 s and ar-19 exited 1 at
#                 t = 99.4 s, each on one aircraft nobody had named - so the run LENGTH, and with it
#                 the ground half's reachability, depended on WHICH aircraft happened to die. With
#                 every aircraft named by the other side, TIMEOUT is structural.
#                 Caps: V <= 24 blue / 12 red (3 x aircraft), M <= 16 blue / 12 red (own `survive` +
#                 own `kill` objectives). MEASURED BELOW as the per-side M actually published.
#   4 ROBUST    - the baseline outcome class survives a spawn perturbation over +-3 m. IT IS NOT
#                 MEASURED HERE AND NOT BUILT TOWARD: S7 is the GATE's screen, and a rung whose
#                 coordinates were chosen so that its own baseline stops moving would be a rung
#                 selected on its own result - the move doc/doctrine-evolution.md has declined five
#                 times. The gate measures it; this file does not anticipate it.
#
# NO RUNG IS A CONTROL OF ANY OTHER. Two coordinates differ between any pair of the twenty, by
# construction, and the set is a SPREAD rather than a factorial: its job is to hand the evolution
# twenty independent cells, never to attribute an effect to daylight, to wind or to any single axis.
#
# THE RANGE IS A GRID ORIGIN, NOT A PLACE. 45.00000 N / 000.00000 E [SET], the same origin as rungs
# 01..10. A coordinate decides exactly two things in this tree - where the sun is and how many metres
# a degree is worth - and this one makes both checkable by eye: at 0 deg of longitude UTC IS local
# apparent solar time, so the clock column is the solar hour angle. `--elev const` on a 0 m datum, no
# terrain masking (gap C4). Scale: 1 deg of latitude = 111 132 m, 1 deg of longitude = 111 320 x
# cos 45 deg = 78 715 m [DERIVED].
#
# THE CAST:
#   BLUE, 8 F-16 in flights of FOUR - four seats deep so that G1's trail levers can
#         act at all: `aftM = element x trail` with `element = (position-1)/2`, so a pair has no
#         second element and two of G1's six levers are unreachable on one (E11 4).
#     ar20str1..4 the STRIKE flight: CCRP, 2 x Mk 84, radar off, one named soft aim point each,
#                  block 2500..2800 m at 450 kt in EVERY rung of the twenty - the ground half is the
#                  arena's constant and carries none of the three new axes.
#     ar20swp1..4 a SWEEP flight: CRM 40 nm, 4 x AIM-7 + 2 x AIM-9, one named MiG each
#   RED, 4 MiG-29 in one flight of four under one GCI brief, 4 x R-73, `n019_emission illum`
#     ar20hi1..4
#   THE GROUND HALF, hostile, and it is in EVERY rung - the arena has no air-only cell:
#     ar20ts1..4   `target_soft`, the four graded aim points, one per striker
#     ar20th1/2    `target_hard`, present and DELIBERATELY UNGRADED. Derivation: the Mk 84's own
#                  fragment law is flux(r) = 2.81e7 / r^2 J/m^2 (sim/missions/mk84-radius.fbm) and
#                  `target_hard`'s structure fails at 9.0e4 (modules/ground/FBGroundTarget.h), so its
#                  fail radius is sqrt(2.81e7 / 9.0e4) = 17.7 m [DERIVED] against a CCRP delivery this
#                  tree lands at 32..87 m [MESS, rungs 01..10]. A graded objective on a hard target
#                  would be a COIN. `target_soft` fails at sqrt(2.81e7 / 2.8e3) = 100.2 m [DERIVED].
#     ar20nod      P-18 early warning, `emcon free` - the net's node and the only ground emitter
#     ar20sam      SA-6, `emcon hold`, 3 rounds     ar20aaa  ZSU-23-4, `emcon hold`, 40 rounds
#     ar20net      the net over the three: wire, period 4.0, hold 3, wcs free, fire units on
#                  `autonomy hold`. A FlightBox battery has NO IFF interrogator, so what it shoots at
#                  is part of the measurement and not a briefing error.
#   THE ASSIGNMENT, and it is a rule rather than a list: each side distributes the OTHER side's
#   aircraft over its own round-robin, so every aircraft is named AT LEAST ONCE and every aircraft
#   names at least one. Where the naming side is the smaller one, the round-robin runs out and the
#   remaining namers repeat a target - so an aircraft is named once or twice, never zero times.
#   Blue names from its sweep flights, red from all of its own.
#   Every callsign is prefixed `ar20`, so the twenty rungs are PAIRWISE DISJOINT in every unit they
#   can lose: the campaign layer's carry has nothing to carry, each rung is measurable standalone,
#   and campaign step k is byte-identical to its own standalone run.
#
# THE GEOMETRY: BEAM (rungs 01..10's geometry C, reused unchanged so that the three NEW axes are
# the only thing this rung adds). Red spawns at 0.58000/0.62000 E and 0.35000 deg =
# 38 896 m NORTH of the blue band, heading 180 - it crosses the corridor from the north instead
# of meeting it, so the aspect at the merge is a beam one. Northing to close 38 896 m, easting
# 41 719 m [DERIVED].
# THE GCI BRIEF IS MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED. Rungs 01..10 derive it from a closure computed on the
# spawn AIRSPEED, which is CALIBRATED airspeed (fdm/FBFdm.cpp: SetVcalibratedKtsIC) and is not the
# ground speed - an error that grows with altitude and would be worst on exactly the high-energy
# rungs this ten adds. So the three calls below are READ OFF a first pass of this very geometry:
# great-circle range and true bearing of the blue sweep lead from the red flight lead at t = 20,
# 60 and 100 s, rounded to the kilometre and the degree the controller would speak
# [MESS, pass 1, --threads 1 --elev const]:
#   t = 20 -> 48 km / 224 deg, t = 60 -> 26 km / 223 deg, t = 100 -> 6 km / 184 deg; blue's block
#   at 12 km.
#
# THE ENERGY (axis 2 of 4.2). The two seats are the tree's OWN, taken from tools/fb_tournament.py's
# GEOMETRIES table rather than invented here: `mirror` is 8000 m / 420 kt on both sides and `split`
# is 12 000 m / 500 kt against 6 000 m / 350 kt - a delta of 12 000 - 6 000 = 6 000 m and
# 500 - 350 = 150 kt [DERIVED], which is verbatim 4.2's own "co-alt/co-speed vs 6,000 m + 150 kt".
# THIS RUNG PUTS BLUE IN THE HIGH SEAT: blue at 12 000 m / 500 kt, red at 6 000 m / 350 kt. BOTH
# directions of the split are in this ten, because 4.2's measurement is that the RANKING inverts
# with the seat, and a single direction would measure the seat rather than the doctrine.
# THE STRIKE FLIGHT DOES NOT CARRY THIS AXIS - it flies 2 500..2 800 m / 450 kt in all twenty rungs.
# The ground half is the arena's constant, so a rung that moves stays comparable in its air half.
#
# THE FORCE RATIO (axis 3 of 4.2). 8 blue against 4 red, i.e. 2:1 - and BOTH graded sides keep
# property 1 (>= 4 aircraft, in flights of four), which is the whole reason the ratio is varied by
# adding and removing FLIGHTS rather than by thinning one to a pair. 4.2's measurement is that the
# cooperative channel is worth an outcome band on an asymmetric cell and nothing on a mirrored one;
# a ratio of 1:1 cannot ask that question, so this ten asks it at four different ratios.
#
# THE WEAPON OBLIGATION (axis 5 of 4.2). [MESS, 4.2] 0.3 s of binding against 17.3 s, a factor of 58;
# the mechanism has no line of code of its own - core/FBStore.h's FBSeekerHandoverS returns the time
# to the round's own activation ring for an ACTIVE seeker, 0 for an INFRARED one and -1 for a
# SEMI-ACTIVE one, and -1 makes weapons/FBStoresSystem keep radiating the uplink for the whole
# predicted time of flight. [MESS, missions/air-eagle-sparrow.fbm against air-eagle-amraam.fbm, one
# geometry, four `set store` lines changed] the shooter is tied to its target for 8.6 s with the
# active round and 39.2 s - to impact - with the semi-active one.
#   BLUE IS BOUND: 4 x AIM-7 (SemiActiveRadar) per sweep aircraft, on the same four stations the
#   AIM-120 rungs use and with the radar, the fuel and the countermeasures unchanged - the ROUND
#   is the only difference. A SemiActiveRadar seeker returns FBSeekerHandoverS -1, so the shooter
#   owes the round illumination all the way to impact.
#   RED IS FREE: 4 x R-73 (Infrared) and NO BVR round - the MiG has to close to fire and is never
#   tied to a round in flight. The N-019 is left exactly as the bound rungs set it (`rad`, 54 nm,
#   `illum`), so what changes between a bound red and a free red is the WEAPON and not the sensor.
#
# THE ATMOSPHERE: `wx wind 9.2 30.9` - one vector at every altitude, deliberately unphysical and
# therefore a measuring instrument rather than weather. THE NUMBERS ARE NOT INVENTED: they are the
# committed GFS fixture's OWN wind at this range's origin at 12 000 m - the block this rung's own
# measurement lives in - restated as a closed form, which is the rule rungs 02/05/09 use.
# [MESS, `build/fb-test-weather assets/wx-2026-07-27T00Z.wxb 45.0 0.0 12000`] windN -15.675 / windE
# -2.535 m/s = 15.879 m/s from 9.187 deg; 15.879 / 0.514444 = 30.87 kt [DERIVED].
#
# MEASURED (2026-07-31, tree 7bd07f0), `fb-gym --mission ... --threads 1 --elev const`:
#   exit 3 (TIMEOUT), run 600.0 s, sun elevation +24.11 deg at the primary actor's spawn point
#   the ground half   4 of 4 releases accepted, 4 deliveries at aimErrM 64.2 / 66.0 / 67.1 / 69.8 m,
#                     4 of 4 soft aim points DESTROYED
#   the air half      off red's rails 4 R-73; off blue's NOTHING
#                     0 warhead detonations, 3 `site LAUNCH` from the belt (no IFF: read
#                     `brgDeg`)
#   the objectives    28 `mission OBJECTIVE` lines, 16 blue and 12 red - property 3 is carried by
#                     MEASUREMENT and not by declaration
#   the outcome class friendly:f16 (V, M) = (20, 12) out of V <= 24, M <= 16;
#                     hostile:mig29 (V, M) = (8, 4) out of V <= 12, M <= 12 - both sides are
#                     graded and neither is inert
#   the GCI brief     is a FIXED POINT of its own run: re-read on the pass it itself drives, the
#                     three calls reproduce to within 0 km and 0 deg
#   determinism       one MD5 over all telemetry*.csv, IDENTICAL at --threads 1, 2 and 4 (9196e3647615),
#                     and the same exit code at all three
#   property 4 (S7)   NOT MEASURED HERE, on purpose - see property 4 above. It is the gate's
#                     screen, and a rung that anticipated it would be a rung selected on its own
#                     result
#   NOTE, and it is a result rather than a defect: BLUE NEVER FIRES AN AIR-TO-AIR ROUND in this
#   rung's baseline. doc/campaigns/ar-arena.md gap AR-5 measured the mechanism on rungs 01..10 -
#   the sweep commands radar STANDBY early under its own emission discipline and never
#   re-radiates - and it is left exactly where it is, because removing it would be tuning the
#   arena on a channel the genome's own EMCON gene acts through.
#
# READING RULE, BINDING. THE EXIT CODE IS NOT THE VERDICT and no reader may quote it as one - every
# rung of this arena is a measuring rig and TIMEOUT (exit 3) is its normal end. THE MEASUREMENT IS THE
# PAIR (V, M) PER GRADED SIDE, computed the way doc/doctrine-evolution.md section 1 computes it: V is
# the sum of the judge's own `UNIT_RESULT` ranks over the side's aircraft (SUCCESS 3, TIMEOUT/NONE 2,
# FAIL 1, CRASH/LOC 0) and M is the number of that side's `mission OBJECTIVE ... state=met` lines.
# Read, in this order: (1) both `mission OBJECTIVE` blocks - if either side publishes none, the rung
# has lost property 3 and nothing else in the file is worth reading; (2) `stores DELIVERY aimErrM`
# against the 100.2 m soft fail radius; (3) `site LAUNCH ... brgDeg` - the belt has no IFF and WHO it
# shot at is a result; (4) the (V, M) pair. A reader who reports a kill count has read a warhead's
# arrival geometry.

